        "raw": "<p>A \"order of play\" question/situation, this time&nbsp;involving Keeper of the Forbidden Wilds, and specifically, these two growth options:</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>Growth Option (2): Add Presence (3 Range) to Land with Wilds or your Presence/Gain 1 Energy</li>\r\n\t<li>Growth Option (3): Pay 3 energy/Gain Power Card/Add Presence (3 Range)&nbsp;to Land Without Blight</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>In all, that's five different \"things\" going on during growth:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>(2)(a) adding presence at 3 range to a land w/ wilds or Keeper's Presence;</li>\r\n\t<li>(2)(b) gaining 1 energy;</li>\r\n\t<li>(3)(a) paying 3 energy;</li>\r\n\t<li>(3)(b)&nbsp;gaining a power card;</li>\r\n\t<li>(3)(c) adding presence (3 range) to a land without blight.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>If you choose these two growth options, can you split up/reorder all 5 \"things\" in whatever order you like, or do all of the \"Option 2\"s have to take place together, and likewise with the \"Option 3\"s?&nbsp; For example, could Keeper:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>Gain a power card (3B)</li>\r\n\t<li>Add Presence (3 range to a land without blight) (3C)</li>\r\n\t<li>Add Presence to land w/wilds or Keeper's Presence; (2A)</li>\r\n\t<li>Gain 1 energy (2B); then</li>\r\n\t<li>Pay 3 energy (3A)?</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p>Or how about within the Options themselves -- can you re-order the \"things\" within each Growth Option?&nbsp; &nbsp;For example, on Keeper's board, the \"Cost 3\" looks like it's attached to the Gain Power Card part; could Keeper first place the Presence, *then* pay the cost/get the power card?</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
