      {
        "id": 223877,
        "name": "robb8888",
        "username": "robb8888",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-10-31T20:34:31.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dpt\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dpt/48/1922_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dpt:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’m pretty sure you need to pay the 3 Energy before you do anything else from that box. I’m not sure why it matters, though: it’s not like placing Presence would give you energy to help pay that cost. Other than that, I’m not sure.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Typically, I try to have Keeper end the turn with 2 Energy in hand, to take Ameena’s suggestion below. &nbsp;What I was hoping to have Keeper do is <em>first</em> use the 3 Range presence option to spread to a land without blight, second, add a second presence there, then gain the energy, then pay the three energy to gain the power card. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>As I understand it from the comments above, though, I have to first add the presence to someplace I already have presence (or wilds), and gain 1 energy (Growth Option <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#3</span>). &nbsp;Only then would&nbsp;I have enough energy for Growth Option <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#4</span>.</p>\n<p>What if (for some reason) it’s super-important for me to instantly plonk down a sacred site somewhere far away? &nbsp;Could I do Growth Option <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#4</span> first, forgo drawing the power card (since I don’t have the energy to pay for it) and just put down a Presence at 3 Range, then use Growth Option <span class=\"hashtag-raw\">#3</span> to add a Presence and gain 1 Energy?</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:57:08.533Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
